{
  "id": "norrie-disease",
  "term": "Norrie disease",
  "definition": "Norrie disease is a disorder caused by mutations that disrupt Norrin signalling, producing severe defects in the retinal blood vessels. These vascular problems lead to visual impairment and can progress to blindness, with ongoing abnormal vessel changes in adulthood linked to persistent low oxygen in the retina.",
